@startuml
!include style.puml
' Orthogonal routing keeps each association on its own vertical, and the leading
' newline in every multiplicity lifts the text clear of the line it labels.
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam arrowThickness 1.1
skinparam arrowColor MODEL_COLOR
skinparam classBackgroundColor MODEL_COLOR

Package Model as ModelPackage <<Rectangle>>{
Class "<<interface>>\nReadOnlyStudentBook" as ReadOnlyStudentBook
Class "<<interface>>\nReadOnlyUserPrefs" as ReadOnlyUserPrefs
Class "<<interface>>\nModel" as Model
Class StudentBook
Class ModelManager
Class UserPrefs

Class UniqueStudentList
Class Student
Class Email
Class Name
Class NusStudentId
Class Phone
Class Tag
Class FollowUpFlag

Class I #FFFFFF
}

Class HiddenOutside #FFFFFF
HiddenOutside ..> Model

StudentBook .up.|> ReadOnlyStudentBook

ModelManager .up.|> Model
Model .right.> ReadOnlyUserPrefs
Model .left.> ReadOnlyStudentBook
ModelManager -left-> "1" StudentBook
ModelManager -right-> "1" UserPrefs
UserPrefs .up.|> ReadOnlyUserPrefs

StudentBook *--> "\n1" UniqueStudentList
UniqueStudentList --> "\n~* all" Student
Student *--> Name
Student *--> "\n0..1" Phone
Student *--> "\n0..1" Email
Student *--> "\n0..1" NusStudentId
Student *--> "\n*" Tag
Student *--> "\n0..1" FollowUpFlag
FollowUpFlag --|> Tag

note right of Student
  isSameStudent compares records by
  NUS Student ID only; a missing ID
  does not establish identity
end note

Student -[hidden]up--> I
UniqueStudentList -[hidden]right-> I

Name -[hidden]right-> Phone
Phone -[hidden]right-> Email
Email -[hidden]right-> NusStudentId

ModelManager --> "\n~* filtered" Student
@enduml

